WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.101 --> 00:00:09.122
Whoosh! Snow sprayed as Kai swerved around a tree.

2
00:00:09.123 --> 00:00:13.746
His skis carved two neat lines down the trail.

3
00:00:13.747 --> 00:00:21.775
It was only an intermediate trail, but it was more difficult than the intermediate trails Kai skied back home in Vermont.

4
00:00:21.776 --> 00:00:27.119
When he reached the bottom, he found his best friend, Zinnia, waiting for him.

5
00:00:27.120 --> 00:00:30.283
"She beat me again!" Kai thought.

6
00:00:30.284 --> 00:00:33.101
He didn't let that bother him though.

7
00:00:33.102 --> 00:00:39.415
Zinnia's aunt and uncle owned the ski resort, so it made sense that she was an accomplished skier.

8
00:00:39.416 --> 00:00:45.665
"You call that an intermediate trail?" Kai said. "That was hard!"

9
00:00:45.666 --> 00:00:53.767
Zinnia laughed. "Every ski resort has its own rating system.

10
00:00:53.768 --> 00:00:59.302
That was an intermediate trail only compared to the other trails at this resort.

11
00:00:59.303 --> 00:01:03.402
Plus, you're used to Vermont's smaller mountains.

12
00:01:03.403 --> 00:01:07.187
We're in Colorado now."

13
00:01:07.188 --> 00:01:13.306
"Right," Kai said. "These mountains are huge!"

14
00:01:13.307 --> 00:01:16.789
"Come on," Zinnia said, taking off.

15
00:01:16.790 --> 00:01:22.074
"Let's check out a more advanced slope—Cliffhanger!"

16
00:01:22.075 --> 00:01:28.881
Kai gulped. "The intermediate trail was already hard," he thought.

17
00:01:28.882 --> 00:01:36.519
"Cliffhanger will probably be way more intense than the advanced slopes that I'm used to back home!"

18
00:01:36.520 --> 00:01:40.924
Kai and Zinnia rode the chairlift up the mountain.

19
00:01:40.925 --> 00:01:49.308
When they got to the top, Kai was a little disappointed, but also relieved—Cliffhanger was closed for maintenance.

20
00:01:49.309 --> 00:01:52.847
"Hey, Zinnia!" A woman walked toward them.

21
00:01:52.848 --> 00:01:58.370
"Hi, Aunt Kate!" Zinnia said before introducing Kai to her aunt.

22
00:01:58.371 --> 00:02:02.592
"Sorry about Cliffhanger," Aunt Kate said.

23
00:02:02.593 --> 00:02:06.126
"It's closed for grooming right now."

24
00:02:06.127 --> 00:02:09.989
Kai was confused. "Grooming?"

25
00:02:09.990 --> 00:02:16.186
Aunt Kate smiled. "That's what we call it when we get trails ready for skiers.

26
00:02:16.187 --> 00:02:20.749
We usually do it at night, but last night was too busy.

27
00:02:20.750 --> 00:02:25.539
Our top priority is always getting the easier trails groomed first.

28
00:02:25.540 --> 00:02:33.585
Fewer people use the advanced trails, so we don't usually bother with them, but they've gotten pretty icy."

29
00:02:33.586 --> 00:02:39.481
Kai looked down the slope and saw machines blowing out thick, powdery white clouds.

30
00:02:39.482 --> 00:02:42.284
"What do those machines do?"

31
00:02:42.285 --> 00:02:46.426
"They're making artificial snow," Aunt Kate said.

32
00:02:46.427 --> 00:02:51.478
"Artificial? Man-made snow?" Kai blinked.

33
00:02:51.479 --> 00:02:54.317
"What's it made out of?"

34
00:02:54.318 --> 00:02:59.647
"It's still just frozen water, like real snow," Zinnia said.

35
00:02:59.648 --> 00:03:09.355
"The ski resort can only earn money a few months each year," Aunt Kate explained, "and some winters we don't get enough snowfall.

36
00:03:09.356 --> 00:03:17.814
We can't afford to close down while we wait for more snow to fall. So we make our own."

37
00:03:17.815 --> 00:03:22.318
"How do the snowmakers work?" Kai asked.

38
00:03:22.319 --> 00:03:25.983
"The process starts with water," Aunt Kate said.

39
00:03:25.984 --> 00:03:33.682
"A special protein that helps ice crystals form is added to the water, which is then pumped up to the machines.

40
00:03:33.683 --> 00:03:40.767
Each machine has several nozzles that shoot water, along with compressed air, into a large fan.

41
00:03:40.768 --> 00:03:47.941
The mixture of water and air sprays out of the fan, freezes, and then falls as snow."

42
00:03:47.942 --> 00:03:53.356
Kai saw a couple of large red vehicles pushing snow downhill.

43
00:03:53.357 --> 00:03:56.712
"Those are our snowcats," Aunt Kate said.

44
00:03:56.713 --> 00:04:05.500
"They groom the slopes by pushing snow into place and smoothing it out, creating a perfect surface for skiers."

45
00:04:05.501 --> 00:04:10.716
"So you can have snow any time of year?" Kai asked.

46
00:04:10.717 --> 00:04:14.388
"Not exactly," Aunt Kate said.

47
00:04:14.389 --> 00:04:20.138
"The temperature still needs to be around freezing for the machines to work properly and efficiently.

48
00:04:20.139 --> 00:04:27.610
But as long as the air isn't too humid, we can make snow even when it’s too warm for snow to fall naturally.

49
00:04:27.611 --> 00:04:31.086
If it's too humid, the water won't freeze.

50
00:04:31.087 --> 00:04:36.989
Artificial snow has even been used in the Winter Olympics since 1980.

51
00:04:36.990 --> 00:04:44.054
The majority of the snow used in the Winter Olympics in Sochi and Pyeongchang was man-made."

52
00:04:44.055 --> 00:04:49.659
"Artificial snow makes a better surface for winter sports," Zinnia said.

53
00:04:49.660 --> 00:04:55.488
"It's more durable and consistent than real snow—it doesn't clump together.

54
00:04:55.489 --> 00:05:01.500
Plus, without artificial snow, we wouldn't be able to go skiing all winter long."

55
00:05:01.501 --> 00:05:08.248
"Not only that," Aunt Kate added, "we wouldn't be able to pay our employees' wages.

56
00:05:08.249 --> 00:05:11.563
The town's economy depends on us.

57
00:05:11.564 --> 00:05:16.448
We don't just have people grooming the slopes and operating the snowmakers.

58
00:05:16.449 --> 00:05:25.750
We also hire people to operate chairlifts, monitor the slopes, and provide skiing and snowboarding lessons."

59
00:05:25.751 --> 00:05:30.915
"Hey!" Zinnia said. "Where are the snowcats going?"

60
00:05:30.916 --> 00:05:37.065
Kai looked down and saw the vehicles driving farther down the mountain.

61
00:05:37.066 --> 00:05:40.723
"They're finished grooming Cliffhanger," Aunt Kate said.

62
00:05:40.724 --> 00:05:46.014
"You two have fun. I'll see you later!"

63
00:05:46.015 --> 00:05:48.627
Zinnia looked at Kai and grinned.

64
00:05:48.628 --> 00:05:53.458
"Ready for your first really big thrill here in Colorado?"

65
00:05:53.459 --> 00:05:56.689
Kai looked down the slope again.

66
00:05:56.690 --> 00:06:02.840
Part of him wished Cliffhanger was still closed—then he wouldn't have to ski down it.

67
00:06:02.841 --> 00:06:05.453
But another part of him was excited.

68
00:06:05.454 --> 00:06:16.813
Kai adjusted his ski goggles. "Let's do it!"

